course: dictionary
lesson: 62
title: Naming success with achievement
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An achievement is something good you managed to do by working hard or using a skill. Look at the context: «be proud of real achievements». The word real tells you these are things people have truly earned.
explain: The word comes from achieve, which means to succeed at a goal. So an achievement is what you have, the result, after you reach something you were aiming for.
explain: You will meet achievement in school, in awards, certificates and progress. Phrases to notice are a great achievement and a sense of achievement, which is the good feeling you get after you reach a goal.
fact: Achievement means something good you managed to do by working hard or being skilful.
fact: Achievement can also mean the act of succeeding or reaching a goal.
fact: «Be proud of real achievements» means feel pleased with things you truly earned.
fact: A sense of achievement is the good feeling you get after reaching a goal.
fact: Achievement can be counted (an achievement, achievements) or used without a count, as an uncountable noun.
exercise: «Wise: be proud of real achievements, check the big words, and when views divide sharply, describe instead of shouting.» What does achievement mean in this sentence? | *Something good you managed to do by working hard | A quiet place to think | A small mistake in your work | A loud argument with friends
exercise: Mia read 50 books this year and her teacher gave her a certificate for it. What is that? | A puzzle | *An achievement | A mistake | A chore
exercise: Find and copy the one word in «be proud of real achievements» that tells you the achievements are truly earned. | *real | be | of | proud
test: Which is the best meaning of achievement? | A type of food | A kind of weather | *Something good you managed to do by working hard | A goal you give up on
test: «She felt a sense of achievement after finishing the race.» What does sense of achievement mean? | *A good feeling after reaching a goal | A feeling of being lost | A feeling of being bored | A feeling of being cold
exam: Which verb is related to achievement and means to succeed at a goal? | *achieve | arrive | ache | believe
